The summary for the class was touched by this PR but still reads "Provides extensions methods for configuring..." The plural modifier should be singular: "extension methods." This is a doc PR, so getting the doc text right is the main deliverable.

::diff{file="src/HttpClientFactory/Polly/src/DependencyInjection/PollyHttpClientBuilderExtensions.cs" lines="14-14"}

The same sentence also contains a leftover "and <see cref=...>" that reads awkwardly, but that predates the PR.

Most of the XML-doc changes are good. Defaults that used to be buried in prose now sit in `<value>` blocks, behavior notes moved to `<remarks>`, and `<see langword="null"/>` and `"true"/"false"` replace plain text. The `MaxDepth` and `FileSizeLimit` rewrites are good examples: the default is visible at a glance and the "why" is in remarks.

::diff{file="src/Validation/src/ValidationOptions.cs" lines="24-35"}

The `ValidateContext` and `SkipValidationAttribute` changes also follow this pattern and read clearly.
